ALVA — Advanced Touch Controls Customization Update

Objective

Implement a complete improvement to ALVA’s touch-control customization system, including:

1. Optional independent control settings for each playable character.
2. Adjustable transparency for individual touch controls.
3. Multi-selection of controls for simultaneous resizing and transparency changes.
4. Movement icons inside the two small circles of the Joystick preview in Settings.
5. A new non-functional Download button in the bottom-right corner of the Home Screen.

Implement these features fully in the existing game, not as mockups or placeholders, except for the Download button, which must intentionally remain non-functional.

Preserve ALVA’s visual identity, existing gameplay, localization, input behavior, and architecture.

⸻

1. Understand the Existing Codebase

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

ALVA is a browser-based 2D platform fighting game built with vanilla JavaScript, HTML, CSS, ES modules, and Canvas 2D. It has no frontend framework or build step.

Before modifying anything, inspect the relevant source code and understand how the existing systems interact.

Important files

* js/core/settings.js — persistent player settings, schema validation, migrations, localStorage.
* js/core/touch-layout.js — control identifiers, position geometry, scale limits, layout sanitization.
* js/ui/touch-layout-editor.js — interactive button layout editor, dragging, selection, resizing, saving, reset.
* js/ui/touch-controls.js — actual gameplay touch buttons, Joystick and Classic schemes, pointer interactions, fighter-specific artwork.
* js/ui/settings-dialog.js — Settings interface, Controls section, scheme preview cards, customization entry point.
* js/screens/battle-screen.js — loading gameplay touch controls for the player’s selected fighter.
* js/screens/practice-screen.js — touch controls and fighter switching during Practice Ground.
* js/screens/home-screen.js — Home Screen buttons and footer.
* js/ui/icons.js — original SVG icon definitions.
* js/data/characters.js — character registry, playable character lookup.
* js/localization/strings/en.js and fr.js — English and French localization.
* css/settings.css — Settings interface and touch editor.
* css/touch-controls.css — touch controls’ appearance.
* css/home.css — Home Screen styling.
* ALVA_SPEC.md — authoritative product specification.
* docs/systems/input.md — touch-control architecture.

The current Settings system uses version 3, with separate Joystick and Classic layouts stored under touchLayouts. Each customized control currently uses { x, y, scale }.

The existing editor supports selecting one control at a time, moving it, resizing it from 70% to 180%, and automatically saving changes.

Extend these systems instead of implementing a separate, competing control editor.

