6. Add a Download Button to the Home Screen

Add one new button with a Download icon in the bottom-right corner of the Home Screen.

Important: this is a future-feature placeholder.

6.1 Positioning

The Home Screen currently has:

* Its main navigation actions.
* Utility buttons in the upper-right corner.
* A bottom footer displaying developer attribution.

Do not add the Download button to the upper-right utility group.

Place it at the bottom right, preferably integrated into the existing Home footer so its position naturally follows the safe-area layout.

It should not overlap the developer attribution, other elements, or the screen’s safe-area insets.

It must remain correctly positioned on desktop and mobile landscape screens.

6.2 Button appearance

Use a compact square icon button consistent with the existing Home Screen utility buttons.

Create a new ICONS.download SVG in js/ui/icons.js.

Use a recognizable download symbol:

* Downward arrow.
* Short horizontal tray or receiving line beneath it.

Follow the existing SVG conventions, including currentColor and the existing icon class.

Use ALVA’s normal charcoal background, subtle border, and off-white/gray icon styling.

The button should feel like an intentional part of the UI, not an unrelated overlay.

6.3 Functionality

The Download button must remain non-functional.

Do not:

* Start any file download.
* Navigate to another page.
* Open a dialog.
* Trigger an alert.
* Introduce a real download URL.
* Add unfinished download logic.

Use a native disabled button or an equivalently accessible non-interactive placeholder, consistent with the Home Screen’s existing disabled Help and Controller buttons.

It must have an accessible localized label such as “Download (coming soon)”.

Because the button is disabled, it must not introduce a broken action into keyboard or gamepad navigation.

Add the corresponding French localization.

